# PART 7 — FEATURE ONE: EVIDENCE TIME MACHINE

Build an interactive timeline replay tool.

Required functionality:
- Display events in chronological order when timestamps are comparable.
- Support search and filters.
- Allow play, pause, next-event, previous-event, and reset.
- Include a draggable timeline position control.
- Show the relevant evidence records as events appear.
- Highlight documented relationships among currently visible entities.
- Display the source evidence ID for each event.
- Clearly separate event time, collection time, and import time.
- Preserve unknown or uncertain timezone information.
- Show possible timestamp conflicts instead of silently resolving them.

When the user changes the replay position, the visible events, selected evidence, and graph context must update.

Include a synthetic scenario where two event timestamps appear inconsistent.

Let users compare:
- The original recorded sequence
- An explicitly labelled hypothetical sequence, if a documented assumption is applied

Never overwrite the original timestamps.

Show the assumption used to produce a hypothetical sequence and allow the user to revert immediately.

Acceptance criterion:
A reviewer can replay a case, select an event, open its source evidence, and inspect a timestamp inconsistency.

